#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133390 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "bb2795c3-6359-50d8-9531-1e9dfae7a2ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-10994" :question/problem "Find $5\\det(A)-\\det(B),$ where \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/65df227e4fff9e934cec11be0a0262a1093a82270f3c9b0b7970fa2c700151aa.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/23865048a3c2ad60dd3b51fe78c44ee368692172300814c3fb061f447266e233.png)\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\det(B) = 3 \\cdot (-4) \\cdot (-2) = 24\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5\\det(A)-\\det(B) = 5 \\cdot 0 - 24 = -24.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "dc780837-b763-5ba9-981a-2373afcb524a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10995" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/d95e60cbfa50178878e719166ace3dbff90c3cc5531acfc046d8354320cd4b00.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has proportional rows: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/3f434912c97c20d04f703253fe41c169497cae82657cfbd0d8b548985549fe64.png)\nAs a result, $|A| = 0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, so \n\n$$\n|B| = (-1) \\cdot 4 \\cdot (-3) = 12 \\neq 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/5f41ff4f7fe5aeae5865bef9ab16d5d97a3513277f70b797c4167882093ed079.png)\nAs a result, $|C| = 0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/id #uuid "33ca37e5-c598-52a2-861f-2d5bfa6fd571" :question/math-academy-id "e-10996" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/ccc50eec6218625f22e8372d6f0b1dbf0da0aa921dff237e4e1b8ea3761bdfc7.png)\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0.$\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows\n\n- $A$ has identical columns" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/2a155f75e1e9c099540eeac555cb20fde5037837d9e5fc9f976bbca15369b51e.png)\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047809/assets/1447045fa5b7875defffdf52d2ae8cf876ee0c5da6ac07cc37bc1c5525fec9c6.png)\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "329589a7-b81d-5e32-a5fa-05463e3daae7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328210} {:answer/id #uuid "4a5b554b-d70d-5cb0-b769-7c6f5bab1e9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328211} {:answer/id #uuid "e55d31f5-dfed-5a23-86c2-cca88b543425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328212} {:answer/id #uuid "7a002fb6-283b-5beb-97ed-b815170a95ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328213} {:answer/id #uuid "c95c7e10-72d0-5fb6-96dd-131041ee658c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e55d31f5-dfed-5a23-86c2-cca88b543425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328212} :answer-field/id #uuid "d256f172-51d9-594b-bf4a-b31d806d4841" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8488a5ef-d0fb-5e97-a97c-9754e4ebd25d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140044" :question/problem "Find $det(A)-3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero row, we obtain:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-3det(B)=0-3\\cdot 0=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf2ce80f-425a-5f81-94c2-2b577e459a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328217} {:answer/id #uuid "517794bf-90c2-52a5-b8c5-803a3117a1d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328218} {:answer/id #uuid "e046d7a7-6981-5d4e-9895-430745cb90f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328219} {:answer/id #uuid "c2df8e23-4502-5058-b902-4880ef765d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328220} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1691fe-902d-5280-9730-d67a6e4f69aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "517794bf-90c2-52a5-b8c5-803a3117a1d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328218} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b2d02b9-5ebe-5fbd-aabd-ce7269173b9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c1bd5a4-43fd-5d63-843c-209b976b49d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-140046" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The $A$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|A|=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1\\cdot 4=8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has identical columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(C)=5\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot (-10)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6d5735-e44b-5798-861a-08fa7d290b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328224} {:answer/id #uuid "dc38cc3f-2361-52ea-98d8-c55218b8d8a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328225} {:answer/id #uuid "9a56992d-bef0-5845-8e64-158cc8be4856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328226} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd98be9-b0cb-575b-94ab-5e3f5e8a6773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328227} {:answer/id #uuid "366280a1-aa2c-5458-9467-45985814efbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfd98be9-b0cb-575b-94ab-5e3f5e8a6773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328227} :answer-field/id #uuid "96ee1707-6e70-5176-86d6-af8065df55ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a49922d8-8419-50d8-9d9c-969ef61c69fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-140047" :question/problem "Find $det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|B|=-1\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-2det(B)=0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a6f6e38-02ff-5c35-99e9-10ca7952deb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328231} {:answer/id #uuid "1b27140f-dfbe-531c-af7d-b66eeb3e8c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328232} {:answer/id #uuid "1ba93eee-ec44-51a7-905e-580af07dc8dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328233} {:answer/id #uuid "0a40f298-309b-5c16-8c06-9283de5d2733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328234} {:answer/id #uuid "9188e2e9-f036-54a2-a37a-442f2c3fa6e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ba93eee-ec44-51a7-905e-580af07dc8dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328233} :answer-field/id #uuid "efe043a2-2621-5064-bbf7-b5e6f8a18ad6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "036c5e8d-bd6c-583c-b82d-de6f4ceb79aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-140050" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns\n- $A$ has identical columns\n- $A$ has identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9217d280-f50a-53b0-bfc2-c0c7677a7699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132351} {:answer/id #uuid "af4d8744-717f-5b80-8929-7c16169609f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132352} {:answer/id #uuid "e464b671-4764-5aea-be6a-a4532655d864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132353} {:answer/id #uuid "ef869476-3fb8-579b-b83e-4b14f4f5a083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132354} {:answer/id #uuid "62aa0ca4-f241-583a-a3e5-8d5a0cfd665d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62aa0ca4-f241-583a-a3e5-8d5a0cfd665d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132355} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b31ae79-ed4f-50ec-a9ed-972b4dfb0966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d571c31-8e0e-520c-b34f-482cf5518003" :question/math-academy-id "q-42458" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n- $A$ has identical columns\n- $A$ has identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8661a1e1-d716-5f53-9cd9-206024b99379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132357} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b9c8df-c2d0-55d3-b669-c1749d8ec665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132358} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a287ff-a881-5cb2-9cce-7753d2448a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132359} {:answer/id #uuid "0b85006e-a881-5d80-a5a4-0ebd37c3209b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132360} {:answer/id #uuid "214cc4ce-0905-59da-8c9f-43565ba8e921" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0b9c8df-c2d0-55d3-b669-c1749d8ec665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132358} :answer-field/id #uuid "64008fe6-8b14-57be-b3db-85cf92537ab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a804e446-7433-50c7-a8ce-2769d7a93237" :question/math-academy-id "q-42459" :question/problem "Find $4det(A)+4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- For the matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-1\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4det(A)+4det(B)=4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 0=12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "830250a7-3bcd-5602-8bcb-ea7012dc6c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328238} {:answer/id #uuid "8bafc66d-163d-5265-a549-91820f45f4b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328239} {:answer/id #uuid "188ce4df-3781-5bf8-ad3a-09b7c8bf4444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328240} {:answer/id #uuid "8e14d12a-0925-52d6-adc9-63674b9f1c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328241} {:answer/id #uuid "1a902147-4cea-5a97-a996-d07c96c4ce1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "830250a7-3bcd-5602-8bcb-ea7012dc6c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328238} :answer-field/id #uuid "a55f4391-a596-51b4-bee4-606c5d3cf1b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee8acf29-78be-5a6d-9c80-499fc4006ff1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42460" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has a zero row\n- $A$ has two proportional columns\n- $A$ has two identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero row.\n\n- $A$ has two proportional columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b891d8e8-a530-544b-b247-5e90aa738fc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328245} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee6dc97-8d73-5771-8f8a-f3b3f5b84fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328246} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd816ac-33d2-5069-a1f9-0960ca12a3d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328247} {:answer/id #uuid "f2416e95-bcbc-5e55-bc32-a423525d319f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328248} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee2c952-978d-5b70-a4f6-603d965be149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b891d8e8-a530-544b-b247-5e90aa738fc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328245} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b612b23-49c1-5a81-b79c-40b3303d76ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "897aeeb1-201c-52b5-9197-9d618dd66f55" :question/math-academy-id "q-42467" :question/problem "Find $3det(A)-4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6\\sqrt{2} & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- For the matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=7\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 4=-5.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6\\sqrt{2} & 10\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-4det(B)=3\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 0=-15.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8005f0ca-4977-5f2a-bd7e-833347dbdfed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$ and $\\mid C \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132435} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d7b997-bde7-5a86-b3fc-46ef4f33deaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid B \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132436} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ebe071-c9f9-5b32-b107-16cee5c17606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$ and $\\mid B \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132437} {:answer/id #uuid "f966effc-ae00-5f69-b8bd-8bc5df80ee28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132438} {:answer/id #uuid "1d2a5166-b0d5-515d-b7b8-55a422f39957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$, $\\mid B \\mid$, and $\\mid C \\mid$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8005f0ca-4977-5f2a-bd7e-833347dbdfed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$ and $\\mid C \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132435} :answer-field/id #uuid "31896ee8-cdd2-5f68-a177-bc3eb837108e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cee2c526-7176-535a-81f7-173bfaefecec" :question/math-academy-id "q-42882" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=1\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=12\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ef4404c-73fd-59d2-807e-4008c6af4d98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328252} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6555fd-6664-5a25-acfe-3c6fd3e45698" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328253} {:answer/id #uuid "dacb2643-442c-5010-8b85-222085b010ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328254} {:answer/id #uuid "05e60e50-44bb-5505-a94d-a1f3e6d1898f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328255} {:answer/id #uuid "623c8d25-6805-541e-a0cd-69a93b98480c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c6555fd-6664-5a25-acfe-3c6fd3e45698" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328253} :answer-field/id #uuid "e00bf8d5-3fb0-58d5-ae66-63e33278e46b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6007578-80c3-5264-817e-c4f8106344f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42958" :question/problem "Find $2det(A)+3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-1)=5\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2det(A)+3det(B)=2\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 0=10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee58a232-2204-5e70-bb6d-6ccec4c0e295" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132441} {:answer/id #uuid "1ffb7cbd-8fe7-5568-a1e6-e64c03f4883f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$, $\\mid B \\mid$, and $\\mid C \\mid$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132442} {:answer/id #uuid "363d3ef9-43eb-590c-9df7-63530f027044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$ and $\\mid C \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132443} {:answer/id #uuid "62351fac-7be9-5cd8-93d6-60f6b5b81dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$ and $\\mid B \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132444} {:answer/id #uuid "7e036bac-5296-59f9-bcab-cac710b32388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid B \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "363d3ef9-43eb-590c-9df7-63530f027044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\mid A \\mid$ and $\\mid C \\mid$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132443} :answer-field/id #uuid "12236104-e892-546a-a842-bbc6bdac3ec2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf123fc4-eb0a-5072-9e49-491e1d68008c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42959" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|B|=3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 5=-15\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328257 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ed38d93-c8dc-559a-ba67-30b614dc45e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328259} {:answer/id #uuid "df723665-7ea2-59e0-b1d8-027118a04750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328260} {:answer/id #uuid "68aecdf5-b4a7-5df9-b9ee-7716bc508f3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328261} {:answer/id #uuid "8125dda9-ce0b-5b57-b56a-98e842c849a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328262} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9dfcf1-eea8-5858-adfc-f9339602f9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df723665-7ea2-59e0-b1d8-027118a04750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328260} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c754a6f-eb1c-5b9c-8014-198c5051bf2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56c75f73-8006-5c39-8150-6ad119a3d555" :question/math-academy-id "q-43058" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{7} & -2\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 4=-40\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{7} & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83cb6ceb-90b8-5e5c-8259-28e92ee386ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132477} {:answer/id #uuid "93025fd8-ddd9-5aca-b9d0-d61347a5b186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132478} {:answer/id #uuid "c778a9d7-0f6e-51a0-8a21-86fe7548cd23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132479} {:answer/id #uuid "084de63e-2eb1-502c-93c8-f747fbec9394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132480} {:answer/id #uuid "0e94b920-5221-5943-85fd-1431a6af28cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83cb6ceb-90b8-5e5c-8259-28e92ee386ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132477} :answer-field/id #uuid "325fa1c2-b096-5ab5-89bc-0c3d016e4b15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ef67ff18-5c70-5c00-bdf0-27b79dc90b72" :question/math-academy-id "q-43306" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ has two identical rows\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- $A$ has two identical columns" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 8-4\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor two identical columns.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09325067-d3bc-5f04-8d3c-42f848520daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328266} {:answer/id #uuid "73432917-0745-51cc-bb2a-a9748f8c9acb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328267} {:answer/id #uuid "e897e5c6-8fe7-5f41-a227-489f0fbebb4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328268} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8f6ba4-d2d7-5c00-a125-3b227b4dcea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328269} {:answer/id #uuid "a34be7d6-e90d-5883-97a1-acfb9835e535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09325067-d3bc-5f04-8d3c-42f848520daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328266} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f7479bf-08b1-5a45-965d-a8bb1206cb98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3957a55d-35bf-5e6d-bbac-473c2a705ba0" :question/math-academy-id "q-82286" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|A|=(-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1=-\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|C|=4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2=-8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48e42694-037c-5360-a9c8-f92825c314fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328273} {:answer/id #uuid "4126f471-03bf-5979-92be-6bbc1eea3888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328274} {:answer/id #uuid "01ed4f45-2049-585e-9daf-fc49b1ae6a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328275} {:answer/id #uuid "c61092d4-96c7-5cb1-9e17-128c4a8ecd51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328276} {:answer/id #uuid "a23ca2dd-156f-5e7a-9a0f-fa4b24abe37d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c61092d4-96c7-5cb1-9e17-128c4a8ecd51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328276} :answer-field/id #uuid "98302e94-fd83-5f8d-a92c-a2a9c9834d4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3127bd8b-ed40-56ad-8355-fdaea133207c" :question/math-academy-id "q-82290" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- $A$ has two identical rows\n- $A$ has a zero row" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor a zero row.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}]}
